            <ArticleTitle>Incidental Liver Findings in 99mTc-Sestamibi Myocardial Perfusion SPECT.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>42-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2967/jnmt.115.158451</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In cardiac nuclear imaging, the liver is mostly remembered as a source of artifact in the left ventricular inferior wall. However, the liver may eventually display unexpected findings, which draw attention to significant noncardiac disease. In a patient referred for myocardial perfusion SPECT to investigate atypical chest pain, focal areas of increased tracer uptake revealed intrahepatic biliary dilatation.</AbstractText>
